WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club

﻿1

00:00:14.123 --> 00:00:16.923
♪ ♪


00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:21.878
Subtitles by explosiveskull


00:00:31.994 --> 00:00:33.929
Quiet!


00:00:41.837 --> 00:00:43.903
What are you?


00:00:43.905 --> 00:00:46.038
Shh.


00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:47.976
Oh.


00:01:02.057 --> 00:01:03.790
You're a demon!


00:01:03.792 --> 00:01:05.791
No, no. I'm not a demon.


00:01:05.793 --> 00:01:07.293
I'm not a demon.


00:01:07.295 --> 00:01:09.129
See? Just a guy.


00:01:09.131 --> 00:01:11.832
Just a guy here to rescue
these dragons, so, uh...


00:01:11.834 --> 00:01:14.201
- But you walked through fire!
- Dragon scales!


00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:15.435
Dragons shed a lot.


00:01:15.437 --> 00:01:17.436
No, I know a demon
when I see one.


00:01:17.438 --> 00:01:18.972
No human legs are that skinny.


00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:23.509
Think that's a good entrance?
Get a load of me.


00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:28.215
I knew it! More demons!


00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.783
Ah, it's really just a nitwit


00:01:29.785 --> 00:01:31.084
who forgot
to fireproof his butt.


00:01:31.086 --> 00:01:32.419
Hot, hot, hot, hot!


00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:34.121
Guys, no, not yet!


00:01:35.757 --> 00:01:38.290
- Behold, your worst nightmare.
- Behold.


00:01:38.292 --> 00:01:40.993
Along with his sister,
who insisted on coming.


00:01:40.995 --> 00:01:42.528
That's my intro?


00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.064
Guys, too soon.
You always come in too soon.


00:01:47.035 --> 00:01:49.902
Sorry, still getting
the hang of my wings.


00:01:49.904 --> 00:01:51.771
Fishlegs, again with the baby?


00:01:53.142 --> 00:01:54.974
- This is a raid.
- I couldn't find a sitter.


00:01:54.976 --> 00:01:56.977
Demons everywhere!


00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:59.079
It's the end of the world!


00:02:00.916 --> 00:02:03.849
: Astrid. I had him
right where I wanted him.


00:02:03.851 --> 00:02:05.951
And now he's right
where I wanted him.


00:02:05.953 --> 00:02:07.120
Let's get to work.


00:02:07.122 --> 00:02:09.021
Okay, we screwed that up,


00:02:09.023 --> 00:02:12.359
but at least nobody else
knows we're here.


00:02:14.463 --> 00:02:16.997
Easy, girl. It's okay.


00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.866
We're gonna get you
out of here.


00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.237
A Crimson Goregutter!


00:02:31.146 --> 00:02:32.945
Look at this weirdo.


00:02:32.947 --> 00:02:34.480
Bet it's super-dumb.


00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:38.117
Why can't I get this cage open?


00:02:38.119 --> 00:02:39.451
It slides.


00:02:39.453 --> 00:02:40.920
Obviously.


00:02:40.922 --> 00:02:42.556
Attack!


00:02:42.558 --> 00:02:45.558
- Get the rescues out of here!
- Get that Night Fury!


00:02:50.231 --> 00:02:51.931
No running on the deck!


00:02:51.933 --> 00:02:53.432
It's slippery.
You could fall.


00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:56.102
Step aside! Let me handle
the tough guy stuff.


00:02:57.138 --> 00:02:58.371
- Huh?
- Whoa.


00:03:00.041 --> 00:03:03.043
Yeah! That's two for me.


00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.414
Look out!


00:03:07.416 --> 00:03:09.449
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no!
- Sorry!


00:03:15.156 --> 00:03:17.924
Ha!


00:03:17.926 --> 00:03:19.359
Thank you.


00:03:19.361 --> 00:03:21.360
Now, go get the rest, bud.


00:03:23.364 --> 00:03:25.497
I thought this was supposed
to be a stealth mission.


00:03:25.499 --> 00:03:27.133
Yeah, they always
start that way.


00:03:27.135 --> 00:03:29.336
Look out!


00:03:31.038 --> 00:03:32.372
Thanks, Stormfly!


00:03:34.343 --> 00:03:36.242
Oh, stop worrying.


00:03:36.244 --> 00:03:37.910
They'll get it.


00:03:41.617 --> 00:03:43.483
Eventually.


00:03:43.485 --> 00:03:45.886
Move out! We got 'em all.


00:03:45.888 --> 00:03:48.021
I'm gonna headlock every last one of you.


00:03:48.023 --> 00:03:50.456
I might even leg-lock you.


00:03:50.458 --> 00:03:52.225
- Let's go, let's go, let's go!
- Amateurs.


00:03:52.227 --> 00:03:54.194
- I was just getting started.
- Clear out, guys!


00:03:54.196 --> 00:03:55.528
Go, go!


00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.465
Don't let them get away!


00:04:01.502 --> 00:04:03.103
Good hustle, boys!


00:04:05.674 --> 00:04:08.144
Toothless, time to go!


00:04:13.581 --> 00:04:15.148
Oh.


00:04:16.317 --> 00:04:18.317
Hey, guys.


00:04:22.223 --> 00:04:25.124
You always have my back, bud.


00:04:30.064 --> 00:04:32.000
♪ ♪


00:04:41.175 --> 00:04:45.612
This is Berk,
your new home away from home.


00:04:45.614 --> 00:04:46.980
A stunning, one-stop,


00:04:46.982 --> 00:04:49.682
all-expense-paid
dream destination.


00:04:51.252 --> 00:04:54.987
So, settle in and let
your worries melt away.


00:04:54.989 --> 00:04:59.127
The service here soars,
the cuisine is fiery...


00:05:01.228 --> 00:05:03.730
...and the locals are
as colorful as you get.


00:05:03.732 --> 00:05:07.701
Any run-of-the-mill paradise
boasts beaches and sunshine.


00:05:09.338 --> 00:05:10.303
Well, not us.


00:05:10.305 --> 00:05:13.740
We've got something
no one else can touch.


00:05:13.742 --> 00:05:17.276
- We, my friend, have dragons.
- Make room!


00:05:17.278 --> 00:05:18.278
They're coming!


00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:22.048
Lots and lots of dragons.


00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:32.992
Gang, meet our latest Berkians.


00:05:34.528 --> 00:05:37.096
Welcome to paradise, mate.


00:05:37.098 --> 00:05:40.033
- Our home is your home.
- Well, aren't you a beauty!


00:05:40.035 --> 00:05:41.567
- Ah, you're welcome. You're welcome.
- Ah.


00:05:41.569 --> 00:05:43.435
I took on, like,
a hundred trappers.


00:05:43.437 --> 00:05:44.771
A-a thousand trappers.


00:05:44.773 --> 00:05:46.605
All with burning undies.


00:05:46.607 --> 00:05:49.608
My thick, full beard almost caught on fire.


00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:52.379
Ugh. Just-just stop.


00:05:52.381 --> 00:05:53.713
So, uh, Hiccup's mom,


00:05:53.715 --> 00:05:55.514
any notes on
my bone-crushing assault,


00:05:55.516 --> 00:05:57.417
or was it pretty much perfect?


00:05:57.419 --> 00:06:00.153
Oh, it was indescribable.


00:06:00.155 --> 00:06:03.122
And please, call me Valka.
It has been a year.


00:06:03.124 --> 00:06:05.257
First-name basis.


00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:07.459
I think the real hero
of the day was Toothless.


00:06:07.461 --> 00:06:09.161
Isn't that right, bud?


00:06:09.163 --> 00:06:11.697
What would we do without you,
oh, king of dragons?


00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:13.399
What would we do?


00:06:13.401 --> 00:06:16.035
Well, we could train
a lot harder, for one.


00:06:16.037 --> 00:06:17.704
That was pretty sloppy.


00:06:17.706 --> 00:06:20.507
Astrid, uh, does have a point.


00:06:20.509 --> 00:06:24.110
Perhaps you all rely a little
bit too much on your dragons


00:06:24.112 --> 00:06:26.245
and not enough on one another.


00:06:26.247 --> 00:06:27.747
See? That's exactly
what I was saying.


00:06:27.749 --> 00:06:29.749
Just listen up, guys.


00:06:29.751 --> 00:06:32.285
Yeah, your mom's
super impressed with me.


00:06:32.287 --> 00:06:34.086
I'm like the son
she always wanted.


00:06:34.088 --> 00:06:35.622
Fishmeat.


00:06:35.624 --> 00:06:38.290
You found a new friend.


00:06:42.364 --> 00:06:43.430
- Mind your heads!
- Whoa! - Oh!


00:07:01.148 --> 00:07:04.684
What good is having
the king of dragons around


00:07:04.686 --> 00:07:06.552
if he can't keep the order?


00:07:06.554 --> 00:07:09.322
Hey, bud, do you want
to do something here or...?


00:07:16.263 --> 00:07:18.665
And where do you suppose
we put these ones?


00:07:18.667 --> 00:07:20.165
Ah, we'll make room.


00:07:21.602 --> 00:07:24.571
You brought back a Hobgobbler!


00:07:24.573 --> 00:07:27.740
They're a bad omen.
We're cursed.


00:07:27.742 --> 00:07:29.274
Nonsense.


00:07:29.276 --> 00:07:31.845
What harm could he do?


00:07:31.847 --> 00:07:32.946
No injuries.


00:07:32.948 --> 00:07:35.848
They're all a little shaken
but otherwise healthy.


00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.884
Now, who's hungry?


00:07:43.124 --> 00:07:46.359
Point is you can't keep
bringing dragons back here.


00:07:46.361 --> 00:07:48.360
Come on, boy.


00:07:48.362 --> 00:07:49.895
You're just asking for trouble.


00:07:49.897 --> 00:07:51.663
No, you don't,
you little thief!


00:07:51.665 --> 00:07:54.200
Those trappers are
getting closer by the day.


00:07:54.202 --> 00:07:56.369
We can handle them.
We have the alpha.


00:07:56.371 --> 00:07:57.870
Ain't that right, bud?


00:07:57.872 --> 00:07:59.639
Would you look at
how happy they are?


00:08:00.442 --> 00:08:03.375
She's awesome.


00:08:03.377 --> 00:08:05.745
Gobber, relax. We did it.


00:08:05.747 --> 00:08:08.347
The world's first
dragon-Viking utopia.


00:08:08.349 --> 00:08:09.883
We made the dream a reality.


00:08:09.885 --> 00:08:13.253
Your dream maybe.
Mine's less crowded and more...


00:08:14.923 --> 00:08:16.788
...sanitary.


00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:18.691
Gobber, you're not
fooling anybody.


00:08:18.693 --> 00:08:19.926
I know you love them.


00:08:24.565 --> 00:08:26.698
You're supposed to be
the generation


00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.168
that leads us into the future.


00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.171
Food fight!


00:08:31.173 --> 00:08:34.506
Ooh, gorgeous.


00:08:34.508 --> 00:08:36.509
- Watch the hair!
- Good, Fishmeat.


00:08:38.579 --> 00:08:41.346
- Ugh! God help us.
- Right between the eyes!


00:08:41.348 --> 00:08:43.950
Time to stop worrying about
problems out there...


00:08:43.952 --> 00:08:45.951
- Gobber.
- ...and start sorting out the ones right here.


00:08:45.953 --> 00:08:47.419
: Okay, okay.


00:08:47.421 --> 00:08:48.654
I-I'll think about it.


00:08:48.656 --> 00:08:51.456
Hang up those saddles
and get married.


00:08:51.458 --> 00:08:53.793
The "M" word.


00:08:53.795 --> 00:08:56.895
Gross. Unless it's me.


00:08:56.897 --> 00:09:00.399
Start ruling like
a proper royal couple.


00:09:00.401 --> 00:09:01.934
Marry him, please.


00:09:01.936 --> 00:09:04.303
You're the only one
with any sense around here.


00:09:04.305 --> 00:09:06.538
With you wearing the pants,
there's still hope.


00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.874
- Wow!
- Gobber...


00:09:07.876 --> 00:09:10.677
Not awkward at all.


00:09:10.679 --> 00:09:12.544
Astrid, don't be like that.


00:09:12.546 --> 00:09:15.215
Whoa. That is a definitive no.


00:09:15.217 --> 00:09:17.649
Look, if you need
a beard to cry on,


00:09:17.651 --> 00:09:19.818
just lean on my shoulder
and you can cry into


00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:21.821
my full, thick beard.


00:09:21.823 --> 00:09:23.690
Oh, thank you, Tuffnut.


00:09:23.692 --> 00:09:25.390
Thank you.


00:09:25.392 --> 00:09:26.960
So much.


00:09:26.962 --> 00:09:28.961
Eret, son of Eret!


00:09:28.963 --> 00:09:31.563
What's the report?


00:09:31.565 --> 00:09:34.234
Two more trapper barges
spotted in the strait.


00:09:34.236 --> 00:09:35.969
So we go after them.


00:09:35.971 --> 00:09:38.004
- What?
- One day,


00:09:38.006 --> 00:09:41.374
you're gonna pick a fight
you can't win.


00:09:41.376 --> 00:09:43.312
♪ ♪


00:10:10.338 --> 00:10:12.038
Archers!


00:10:17.846 --> 00:10:20.712
- Dragon killers.
- Stay on your guard.


00:10:20.714 --> 00:10:22.650
Deathgrippers.


00:10:35.863 --> 00:10:38.597
Back! Do what I say, now!


00:10:38.599 --> 00:10:40.566
Do what I say!


00:10:40.568 --> 00:10:43.302
Grab the other head
on that Zippleback!


00:10:43.304 --> 00:10:44.637
You belong to the...


00:10:44.639 --> 00:10:47.407
The dragon riders
attacked us here,


00:10:47.409 --> 00:10:48.841
off the Eastern Strait.


00:10:50.878 --> 00:10:53.046
- Ragnar.
- Um, sorry.


00:10:53.048 --> 00:10:55.380
My dear warlords.


00:10:55.382 --> 00:10:59.485
How go your plans
to conquer the world?


00:11:01.088 --> 00:11:04.023
Grimmel, my old friend.


00:11:04.025 --> 00:11:05.357
Thank you for coming.


00:11:05.359 --> 00:11:07.326
Oh!


00:11:07.328 --> 00:11:09.961
A year since Drago's defeat,


00:11:09.963 --> 00:11:13.799
and no further along
with your dragon army, I see.


00:11:13.801 --> 00:11:16.436
You can thank the young chief
of Berk for that.


00:11:16.438 --> 00:11:18.104
Stoick's boy?


00:11:18.106 --> 00:11:21.673
Yep, he and his
peace-loving dragon riders


00:11:21.675 --> 00:11:25.577
continue to raid our ships
and steal our dragons.


00:11:25.579 --> 00:11:28.114
Mm. That does sound
like a nuisance.


00:11:28.116 --> 00:11:30.350
But I'm in the business
of killing dragons,


00:11:30.352 --> 00:11:32.351
not retrieving them.


00:11:32.353 --> 00:11:34.519
- But, Grimmel...
- That idiot boy has done


00:11:34.521 --> 00:11:35.955
all of the work for you,


00:11:35.957 --> 00:11:38.390
gathering the dragons
in one place.


00:11:38.392 --> 00:11:39.759
Why bother me?


00:11:39.761 --> 00:11:43.432
Because the flock is protected
by a Night Fury.


00:11:47.434 --> 00:11:48.934
Not possible.


00:11:48.936 --> 00:11:52.904
It seems one slipped
through your fingers.


00:11:52.906 --> 00:11:56.609
Look, Berk's dragons
will follow the alpha.


00:11:56.611 --> 00:12:01.947
So we'll pay you to capture him
and bring the flock to us.


00:12:01.949 --> 00:12:04.752
: We even have
your favorite bait.


00:12:07.822 --> 00:12:11.090
The only dragon they left us
from last night's raid.


00:12:11.092 --> 00:12:14.626
A female? Hmm.


00:12:16.397 --> 00:12:20.099
So, do we have a deal,
old friend?


00:12:23.737 --> 00:12:24.872
Watch out!


00:12:33.948 --> 00:12:36.014
When all is said and done,


00:12:36.016 --> 00:12:39.684
this young chief will
bring me the Night Fury.


00:12:39.686 --> 00:12:45.393
They don't have a leader,
just a boy.


00:12:47.495 --> 00:12:49.796
Hiccup.


00:12:52.099 --> 00:12:55.467
This is Berk, son.


00:12:55.469 --> 00:12:57.637
It's our home.


00:12:57.639 --> 00:12:59.938
It was the home
of your grandparents


00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.674
and their grandparents
before them.


00:13:02.676 --> 00:13:06.678
And it's my job as chief
to protect us, Hiccup.


00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.980
And one day,
when you're all grown up,


00:13:08.982 --> 00:13:11.149
that job will be
passed on to you.


00:13:11.151 --> 00:13:12.884
Okay.


00:13:12.886 --> 00:13:16.221
And it's very important, son,
because out there,


00:13:16.223 --> 00:13:20.993
beyond the sunset,
lies the home of the dragons.


00:13:20.995 --> 00:13:23.962
- Wow.
- Aye.


00:13:23.964 --> 00:13:27.200
Legends tell of ships
that sailed too close to it,


00:13:27.202 --> 00:13:29.936
only to drop off
the edge of the world,


00:13:29.938 --> 00:13:32.804
never to be seen again.


00:13:32.806 --> 00:13:35.006
But those sailors
who turned back


00:13:35.008 --> 00:13:37.943
told tales of a great waterfall


00:13:37.945 --> 00:13:41.514
and dragons guarding
the entrance to a Hidden World.


00:13:41.516 --> 00:13:44.517
- Whoa.
- Not just a nest, Hiccup,


00:13:44.519 --> 00:13:47.986
but a land from which
all dragons come.


00:13:47.988 --> 00:13:50.822
Even Night Furies?


00:13:50.824 --> 00:13:52.624
Especially Night Furies.


00:13:52.626 --> 00:13:55.061
Those are scary.


00:13:55.063 --> 00:13:56.596
Don't you worry.


00:13:56.598 --> 00:13:59.532
One day, I'll find
the Hidden World


00:13:59.534 --> 00:14:01.701
and seal it up,


00:14:01.703 --> 00:14:05.641
so that people and dragons
will fight no more.


00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:17.517
What?


00:14:18.953 --> 00:14:20.686
Oh, all right.


00:14:20.688 --> 00:14:22.989
You do know it's not
a chew toy, don't you?


00:14:22.991 --> 00:14:25.258
Is this what you want?
Oh, do you want this leg?


00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.763
Do you want my leg?
Go get it.


00:14:39.306 --> 00:14:42.143
Getting pretty good
at gliding on your own, bud.


00:14:55.256 --> 00:14:59.057
Oh, so this is where you come
to get away from Gobber.


00:14:59.059 --> 00:15:01.863
I have no idea
what you're talking about.


00:15:03.631 --> 00:15:06.097
Ugh.


00:15:06.099 --> 00:15:07.799
Well, he's right, you know.


00:15:07.801 --> 00:15:09.668
R-Really?


00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.770
You think you and I should...?


00:15:11.772 --> 00:15:13.038
Oh, gods, no.


00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.041
We're nowhere near
ready for that.


00:15:15.043 --> 00:15:17.043
No, that's-that's crazy.


00:15:17.045 --> 00:15:19.845
I mean, he's right
about all of this.


00:15:19.847 --> 00:15:23.982
It does seem like the
whole world knows about us now.


00:15:23.984 --> 00:15:26.351
Yep. And the more dragons
we bring back here,


00:15:26.353 --> 00:15:28.754
the bigger of a target
we become.


00:15:28.756 --> 00:15:29.989
Ugh.


00:15:29.991 --> 00:15:34.225
I just wish there was some way
to make them leave us alone.


00:15:34.227 --> 00:15:35.796
There might be.


00:15:37.899 --> 00:15:41.232
Dad used to talk about
an old mariners' myth,


00:15:41.234 --> 00:15:43.769
of a secret land
at the edge of the world


00:15:43.771 --> 00:15:46.038
where dragons live
totally out of reach.


00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:50.042
Well, sailors are
known for tall tales.


00:15:50.044 --> 00:15:53.078
True. But what if it's real?


00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:56.115
It could be the answer
to all of our problems.


00:15:56.117 --> 00:15:59.652
How? By moving
the dragons there?


00:15:59.654 --> 00:16:02.388
Uh-uh. All of us.


00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.222
Seriously?


00:16:04.224 --> 00:16:07.793
And abandon our home
of seven generations?


00:16:07.795 --> 00:16:11.197
The home your father left you to protect.


00:16:11.199 --> 00:16:12.764
Uh...


00:16:12.766 --> 00:16:14.899
Yeah, I think we need
a real solution, Hiccup.


00:16:20.642 --> 00:16:22.642
Well, we could just
take Gobber's advice


00:16:22.644 --> 00:16:23.875
and tie the knot.


00:16:23.877 --> 00:16:25.877
That should fix everything.


00:16:25.879 --> 00:16:28.780
But, hey, if you're having
doubts about yours truly,


00:16:28.782 --> 00:16:31.150
I'm pretty sure Snotlout's available.


00:16:31.152 --> 00:16:33.352
He only has eyes for your mom.


00:16:35.723 --> 00:16:38.657
- Playing dirty now, huh?
- You asked for it.


00:16:38.659 --> 00:16:41.160
Looks like there might be
a wedding after all.


00:16:41.162 --> 00:16:44.329
Oh, how dare you? That is a low blow.


00:16:44.331 --> 00:16:47.032
No, no, you are not
getting away.


00:16:47.034 --> 00:16:49.268
Okay, okay, you win, you win!


00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.836
You always win.


00:16:51.838 --> 00:16:53.705
You knew what you were
getting into.


00:16:53.707 --> 00:16:56.043
Uh-huh. Right.


00:17:01.782 --> 00:17:03.217
Uh, bud?


00:17:06.953 --> 00:17:09.954
What... Yeah, sure,
don't bother to wait for us.


00:17:40.088 --> 00:17:41.990
♪ ♪


00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:04.435
Oh, my gods.


00:19:04.437 --> 00:19:06.172
Uh, Hiccup!


00:19:06.174 --> 00:19:08.109
Oh!


00:19:12.346 --> 00:19:14.913
Yeah, yeah, w-we're friends.
No need to kill us.


00:19:34.367 --> 00:19:36.935
-: Wow.
- Another Night Fury.


00:19:36.937 --> 00:19:39.838
No, not quite.
It's more like a...


00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:42.607
- Bright... Fury.
- A Light Fury.


00:19:42.609 --> 00:19:45.310
Yeah, yours is better,
probably.


00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.614
<i>What do you mean, gone?</i>


00:19:48.616 --> 00:19:50.915
Vanished, into thin air.


00:19:50.917 --> 00:19:53.117
- What do you think?
- Uh-uh.


00:19:53.119 --> 00:19:54.987
Stubbier ears.
No dorsal plates.


00:19:54.989 --> 00:19:56.488
Okay. Got it.


00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:58.324
What a night.


00:19:58.326 --> 00:20:00.192
Bud, what's gotten into you?


00:20:00.194 --> 00:20:02.528
What is all this
slobbering and panting?


00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:06.899
Isn't it obvious?
He's in love.


00:20:06.901 --> 00:20:09.969
Trust me, relationships are
nothing but pain and misery.


00:20:11.305 --> 00:20:13.605
What did I just say?


00:20:13.607 --> 00:20:15.340
A-Am I not enough?


00:20:17.377 --> 00:20:19.278
I think that's a no.


00:20:31.091 --> 00:20:33.157
- Something like this?
- You know what?


00:20:33.159 --> 00:20:34.593
Just trace your Toothless card
and make her white.


00:20:34.595 --> 00:20:36.528
- You could've led with that.
- Can you believe it?


00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.529
Toothless has a girlfriend.


00:20:38.531 --> 00:20:40.566
I never took you
for a romantic.


00:20:40.568 --> 00:20:42.101
Like, ever.


00:20:42.103 --> 00:20:44.068
But it's so sweet.


00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:46.471
I mean, look.


00:20:54.214 --> 00:20:56.015
Okay. That's just sad.


00:20:56.017 --> 00:20:58.517
- And weird.
- Yeah, you better do something.


00:20:58.519 --> 00:21:02.121
Seriously? I'd rather shovel
poop all day than watch that.


00:21:02.123 --> 00:21:04.123
All right.
Let's head back to the woods


00:21:04.125 --> 00:21:05.559
and see if we can find her.


00:21:08.963 --> 00:21:10.229
Ah, good idea.


00:21:10.231 --> 00:21:11.563
A little privacy.


00:21:11.565 --> 00:21:13.298
- Uh...
- Shh.


00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.666
- It's boy talk.
- What?


00:21:14.668 --> 00:21:17.336
Come on,
let's go work this out.


00:21:17.338 --> 00:21:18.636
So, you want to get married.


00:21:18.638 --> 00:21:20.172
Uh, no, actually.


00:21:20.174 --> 00:21:22.074
Good news.
I've been to two weddings.


00:21:22.076 --> 00:21:25.944
I crashed both, but none
as high profile as this one.


00:21:25.946 --> 00:21:28.579
Lots of pressure, judgment,
and not just by me.


00:21:28.581 --> 00:21:31.115
Look, we talked about it.
We're not getting married.


00:21:31.117 --> 00:21:33.719
Cold feet.
I've seen it before.


00:21:33.721 --> 00:21:36.989
Don't worry, Little Hiccy.
I'm here.


00:21:36.991 --> 00:21:38.457
Wait, Hiccy?


00:21:38.459 --> 00:21:40.459
Now, I've seen the way
Astrid looks at you.


00:21:40.461 --> 00:21:41.993
Everyone has. That doubt.


00:21:41.995 --> 00:21:43.429
That not so subtle
disappointment.


00:21:43.431 --> 00:21:46.432
That longing for something
more than you.


00:21:46.434 --> 00:21:48.334
You need to focus on
being worthy.


00:21:48.336 --> 00:21:50.336
I mean, she's a warrior queen,
for Thor's sake.


00:21:50.338 --> 00:21:53.338
And you are neither.


00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:55.039
But with me as your best man...


00:21:55.041 --> 00:21:56.709
your spirit guide,
if you will...


00:21:56.711 --> 00:21:59.711
you'll learn to embrace
your inner Viking.


00:21:59.713 --> 00:22:01.713
Show these naysayers,
of which there are many,


00:22:01.715 --> 00:22:05.150
that you're more than
just a malnourished runt


00:22:05.152 --> 00:22:07.752
with bad hair, strange teeth,
and a twig for a neck.


00:22:07.754 --> 00:22:10.722
You're-you're
really bad at pep talks.


00:22:10.724 --> 00:22:12.691
Stop letting these insecurities


00:22:12.693 --> 00:22:14.292
get the best of you.


00:22:14.294 --> 00:22:16.461
Everyone's watching.
I mean, everyone.


00:22:16.463 --> 00:22:18.463
You need to man up.
Do as I do.


00:22:18.465 --> 00:22:21.567
It'll be hard,
but you have my word.


00:22:21.569 --> 00:22:24.737
And until I break that word,
I won't give up.


00:22:24.739 --> 00:22:26.637
Hey.


00:22:26.639 --> 00:22:29.441
Hey! What, am I wasting
my time here?


00:22:29.443 --> 00:22:33.114
You see some shiny thing in
the woods... Ooh, what is that?


00:22:42.490 --> 00:22:45.324
Toothless!


00:22:45.326 --> 00:22:47.058
Don't move a muscle.


00:22:47.060 --> 00:22:49.297
Hey!


00:22:58.039 --> 00:22:59.538
- Someone's here.
- Huh?


00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:01.205
He managed to slip
past our scouts


00:23:01.207 --> 00:23:02.673
and lay a trap in the woods.


00:23:02.675 --> 00:23:05.510
- It ruined boy talk.
-: Oh.


00:23:05.512 --> 00:23:07.779
- Gah, let me at him!
- Slow down, Gobber.


00:23:07.781 --> 00:23:10.615
Let's get a search team on
the ground, scouts in the air.


00:23:10.617 --> 00:23:12.651
Toothless and I
will fly the coastline.


00:23:12.653 --> 00:23:16.622
Yeah, I wouldn't advise taking
Toothless anywhere, Chief.


00:23:16.624 --> 00:23:18.790
I know this handiwork.


00:23:18.792 --> 00:23:22.126
Grimmel the Grisly.
Famous back where I'm from.


00:23:22.128 --> 00:23:24.430
The smartest dragon hunter
I ever met.


00:23:24.432 --> 00:23:26.531
Well, next to me, of course.


00:23:26.533 --> 00:23:29.734
Well, he can't be that smart.
He left his trap unmanned.


00:23:29.736 --> 00:23:34.073
Nothing's accidental
when it comes to old Grimmel.


00:23:34.075 --> 00:23:35.740
He lives for the hunt,


00:23:35.742 --> 00:23:37.742
to get inside the mind
of his prey,


00:23:37.744 --> 00:23:40.211
to control its every choice.


00:23:40.213 --> 00:23:41.779
It's all a game to him.


00:23:41.781 --> 00:23:43.714
Well, he doesn't know
who he's playing with.


00:23:43.716 --> 00:23:45.717
Yeah. Well, we've dealt with
his kind before.


00:23:45.719 --> 00:23:47.752
Don't underestimate him,
Hiccup.


00:23:47.754 --> 00:23:50.489
Mark my words.
He'll be back.


00:23:50.491 --> 00:23:53.094
Then we'll be waiting for him.


00:24:06.373 --> 00:24:07.839
All right.


00:24:07.841 --> 00:24:10.241
All right, come on,
give me a clue here.


00:24:10.243 --> 00:24:12.414
Give me a clue, Dad.


00:24:33.367 --> 00:24:36.236
Oh, I hope you don't mind
if I help myself.


00:24:38.239 --> 00:24:40.175
This is, uh, mmm, quite good.


00:24:41.876 --> 00:24:45.280
Oh, that is impressive.
But let me finish my drink.


00:24:49.183 --> 00:24:50.117
Toothless!


00:24:53.287 --> 00:24:55.621
What did you do to him?


00:24:55.623 --> 00:24:58.557
Eh, nothing
that he won't sleep off.


00:25:01.794 --> 00:25:03.162
May I?


00:25:03.164 --> 00:25:04.297
Chief Hiccup.


00:25:04.299 --> 00:25:08.333
Hmm? Do I say Chief
or do I call you Hiccup?


00:25:08.335 --> 00:25:09.604
What do you prefer?


00:25:11.405 --> 00:25:16.307
You have no idea
who I am, do you?


00:25:16.309 --> 00:25:18.176
Oh.


00:25:18.178 --> 00:25:20.412
Well, your father knew of me.


00:25:20.414 --> 00:25:23.315
Now, there was a chief.


00:25:23.317 --> 00:25:27.920
One of the greatest dragon
hunters to have ever lived.


00:25:27.922 --> 00:25:30.489
What would he think of you?


00:25:33.927 --> 00:25:35.626
He had it right, you know.


00:25:35.628 --> 00:25:37.628
Making it his mission
to destroy the beasts


00:25:37.630 --> 00:25:39.897
so that you could grow up
in a better world.


00:25:39.899 --> 00:25:41.866
He changed his mind.


00:25:41.868 --> 00:25:44.238
And look where that got him.


00:25:45.739 --> 00:25:48.941
So let's get to the point.


00:25:48.943 --> 00:25:51.643
I am the Night Fury killer.


00:25:51.645 --> 00:25:56.214
I've hunted
every last one but yours.


00:25:56.216 --> 00:25:58.817
You are going to give me
that dragon, or I will...


00:25:58.819 --> 00:26:00.719
I will never give him up.


00:26:02.889 --> 00:26:07.728
You wish dragons to live free
among us like equals?


00:26:09.597 --> 00:26:11.797
A toxic notion, my boy.


00:26:11.799 --> 00:26:15.433
History has shown that we are
the superior species.


00:26:15.435 --> 00:26:19.904
What if word of your
misguided ideas were to spread?


00:26:19.906 --> 00:26:23.008
It would be the undoing
of civilization


00:26:23.010 --> 00:26:26.545
as we know it.


00:26:26.547 --> 00:26:28.482
Hmm.


00:26:32.319 --> 00:26:34.556
Did we get him?


00:26:36.723 --> 00:26:37.692
Now!


00:26:39.827 --> 00:26:41.393
Sorry to barge in.


00:26:41.395 --> 00:26:44.328
You think you can
come into my home,


00:26:44.330 --> 00:26:48.499
sit in my father's chair,
and threaten my dragon?


00:26:48.501 --> 00:26:50.469
This is Berk.


00:26:50.471 --> 00:26:53.971
And we have defended our way of
life from far worse than you.


00:26:53.973 --> 00:26:55.740
Ooh.


00:26:55.742 --> 00:26:58.676
A fighting spirit.
I love it.


00:26:58.678 --> 00:27:02.013
Only I'm afraid
you're mistaken.


00:27:02.015 --> 00:27:05.651
You've never seen
anything like me.


00:27:14.728 --> 00:27:15.930
Astrid, look out!


00:27:23.037 --> 00:27:25.037
Look out! Son, get clear.


00:27:27.374 --> 00:27:29.309
Run!


00:27:36.649 --> 00:27:38.950
Have my dragon ready


00:27:38.952 --> 00:27:43.958
when I return, or I will
destroy everything you love.


00:27:51.565 --> 00:27:55.400
- Grab the buckets!
- How did this happen?!


00:27:57.338 --> 00:27:59.337
- Inside.
- It's the middle of the night.


00:27:59.339 --> 00:28:01.605
- What are we doing here?
- All right.


00:28:01.607 --> 00:28:04.378
All right, everybody.
Settle down, please.


00:28:05.511 --> 00:28:07.412
Fishlegs.


00:28:07.414 --> 00:28:09.847
Have you ever seen
that species of dragon before?


00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:13.785
Let me at him!


00:28:13.787 --> 00:28:15.619
I'll give him
a piece of my mind!


00:28:15.621 --> 00:28:18.423
And by mind, I mean fist!


00:28:18.425 --> 00:28:20.925
Did you miss the part
where we almost died?


00:28:20.927 --> 00:28:23.561
Have you seen my house?


00:28:23.563 --> 00:28:26.030
This is a new kind of enemy.


00:28:26.032 --> 00:28:28.700
And I underestimated him.
Now, that's on me.


00:28:28.702 --> 00:28:30.701
But I will not do that again.


00:28:30.703 --> 00:28:33.939
We're Vikings.
We don't run from a fight.


00:28:33.941 --> 00:28:36.040
At least, I don't.
You might.


00:28:36.042 --> 00:28:37.909
I agree with Hiccup.


00:28:37.911 --> 00:28:39.911
We haven't seen
the last of Grimmel.


00:28:39.913 --> 00:28:42.814
He's a predator,
single-minded and patient.


00:28:42.816 --> 00:28:44.982
He won't stop
until he gets what he wants.


00:28:44.984 --> 00:28:46.084
I'm with Eret.


00:28:46.086 --> 00:28:49.086
We have to take
this threat seriously.


00:28:49.088 --> 00:28:51.088
Grimmel is just
a sign of the times.


00:28:51.090 --> 00:28:54.526
Our enemies are getting
smarter, more determined.


00:28:54.528 --> 00:28:58.963
We're not just overcrowded.
We are exposed and vulnerable.


00:28:58.965 --> 00:29:02.567
Short of full-blown war
and risking everyone we love,


00:29:02.569 --> 00:29:05.836
I don't...


00:29:05.838 --> 00:29:09.173
I don't see a way
of staying here any longer.


00:29:09.175 --> 00:29:10.942
What would Stoick think of this?


00:29:10.944 --> 00:29:13.513
Hey! Hear him out!


00:29:19.586 --> 00:29:22.921
If we want to live in peace
with our dragons,


00:29:22.923 --> 00:29:24.955
we need a better plan.


00:29:24.957 --> 00:29:27.659
So what are you saying, Chief?


00:29:27.661 --> 00:29:29.827
I'm saying
we have to disappear.


00:29:29.829 --> 00:29:31.762
Off the map.


00:29:31.764 --> 00:29:34.999
Take the dragons to a place
where no one will find them.


00:29:35.001 --> 00:29:37.001
And where might that be?


00:29:37.003 --> 00:29:39.837
He's talking about a quest
for the Hidden World.


00:29:39.839 --> 00:29:40.705
The hidden what?


00:29:40.707 --> 00:29:42.840
Out to lunch. - Yeah.


00:29:42.842 --> 00:29:45.844
My father was obsessed with it
when I was a boy.


00:29:45.846 --> 00:29:47.612
He made notes and maps


00:29:47.614 --> 00:29:51.450
in search of the ancestral home
of all dragons,


00:29:51.452 --> 00:29:54.685
tucked away somewhere
beyond the edge of the world.


00:29:54.687 --> 00:29:56.821
It may be the solution we need.


00:29:56.823 --> 00:29:59.657
We are dragon people.


00:29:59.659 --> 00:30:01.759
It's where we belong.


00:30:01.761 --> 00:30:05.763
Look, I know this is our home.


00:30:05.765 --> 00:30:08.532
My father left me
to protect it.


00:30:08.534 --> 00:30:11.536
But Berk is more
than this place.


00:30:11.538 --> 00:30:13.471
We are Berk.


00:30:13.473 --> 00:30:15.105
The people, the dragons.


00:30:15.107 --> 00:30:18.876
I say Berk is wherever we go.


00:30:18.878 --> 00:30:20.211
I don't know.


00:30:20.213 --> 00:30:21.579
What do you think?


00:30:21.581 --> 00:30:24.583
I'm with him! Who else?!


00:30:24.585 --> 00:30:26.585
♪ ♪


00:30:43.669 --> 00:30:45.069
Excuse me. Coming through.


00:30:45.071 --> 00:30:47.172
Just, let me just
get right through here.


00:30:47.174 --> 00:30:51.009
Fishmeat, look, eat your rocks.
Eat your rocks.


00:30:51.011 --> 00:30:53.511
Gods! People who fly
with babies are the worst.


00:30:55.682 --> 00:30:58.249
I feel like I'm always asking
you this question, but...


00:30:58.251 --> 00:31:00.251
Wake up, Grump! Wake up!


00:31:00.253 --> 00:31:02.653
Is there an actual plan or...?


00:31:02.655 --> 00:31:05.757
Just keep flying until
we reach the end of the world.


00:31:05.759 --> 00:31:08.226
Ah. Seems sensible.


00:31:08.228 --> 00:31:11.028
<i>So, where are they?</i>


00:31:11.030 --> 00:31:12.963
Gone. Obviously.


00:31:12.965 --> 00:31:15.099
The Night Fury escaped you?


00:31:15.101 --> 00:31:17.269
- Again?
- I encouraged it.


00:31:17.271 --> 00:31:20.704
They've abandoned
their only defensible position.


00:31:20.706 --> 00:31:22.307
<i>Running scared</i>


00:31:22.309 --> 00:31:24.709
<i>with what little
they can carry.</i>


00:31:24.711 --> 00:31:26.611
It just keeps going.


00:31:26.613 --> 00:31:29.314
That's 'cause the world
is actually round.


00:31:29.316 --> 00:31:30.915
The sun's round. The moon is round.


00:31:30.917 --> 00:31:32.284
Stars are round.


00:31:32.286 --> 00:31:34.118
Even though
they're small and stupid.


00:31:34.120 --> 00:31:37.154
Right? Stars.


00:31:37.156 --> 00:31:39.324
Don't fret.
They won't get far.


00:31:39.326 --> 00:31:42.594
The Night Fury is distracted.


00:31:42.596 --> 00:31:46.298
I introduced him
to your female.


00:31:46.300 --> 00:31:48.299
<i>Furies mate for life, you see.</i>


00:31:48.301 --> 00:31:51.169
What you picking up on, bud?


00:31:53.272 --> 00:31:54.772
The Light Fury!


00:31:54.774 --> 00:31:56.173
- She's following us!
- Wow!


00:31:56.175 --> 00:31:58.175
Cool.


00:32:00.213 --> 00:32:02.212
- Would ya look at that?
- Where'd she go?


00:32:02.214 --> 00:32:04.182
Is she made of sky?


00:32:04.184 --> 00:32:06.521
Whoa! Hold up, Toothless!


00:32:12.925 --> 00:32:15.326
Well, look who it is.


00:32:15.328 --> 00:32:18.028
Uh...


00:32:18.030 --> 00:32:19.663
Oh, hey, it's really nice
to finally...


00:32:31.144 --> 00:32:34.346
This is perfect. So great.


00:32:34.348 --> 00:32:36.183
Not a word.


00:32:39.019 --> 00:32:40.986
<i>Y-Yes, yes,
but where did they go?</i>


00:32:40.988 --> 00:32:43.622
I have to explain this.


00:32:43.624 --> 00:32:46.290
Night Furies can't survive
in the cold,


00:32:46.292 --> 00:32:47.526
so they haven't gone north.


00:32:47.528 --> 00:32:49.627
<i>They're trying to put distance
between themselves</i>


00:32:49.629 --> 00:32:50.996
<i>and enemies to the east</i>


00:32:50.998 --> 00:32:52.329
and south.


00:32:52.331 --> 00:32:54.164
<i>And Night Furies cannot fly</i>


00:32:54.166 --> 00:32:57.902
<i>long distances without rest.</i>


00:32:57.904 --> 00:33:00.372
Their flight path
must include stops.


00:33:00.374 --> 00:33:01.776
Potty break!


00:33:03.676 --> 00:33:06.411
<i>Therefore, they've gone...</i>


00:33:08.415 --> 00:33:11.184
<i>They can only have gone...</i>


00:33:13.252 --> 00:33:16.721
<i>Does anyone want
to take a guess?</i>


00:33:16.723 --> 00:33:18.155
Anyone?


00:33:18.157 --> 00:33:20.157
W-W... W-W-W...


00:33:20.159 --> 00:33:22.292
Ah, east!


00:33:22.294 --> 00:33:24.029
West.


00:33:24.031 --> 00:33:26.865
Hmm? Simple, you see?


00:33:26.867 --> 00:33:28.866
Oh, isn't this fun?


00:33:28.868 --> 00:33:31.035
Yes? No?


00:33:32.705 --> 00:33:35.006
Yes. Yes.


00:33:35.008 --> 00:33:37.341
Where is your love of the hunt?


00:33:37.343 --> 00:33:39.877
I thought you were conquerors.


00:33:39.879 --> 00:33:42.080
You'll have your prize in time.


00:33:42.082 --> 00:33:47.051
Just allow me a few more days
to enjoy this.


00:33:47.053 --> 00:33:49.053
I have dearly missed it.


00:33:49.055 --> 00:33:50.689
<i>All right.</i>


00:33:50.691 --> 00:33:52.857
Looks like we're camping here
for tonight.


00:33:52.859 --> 00:33:54.825
Well, thank Thor for that.


00:33:54.827 --> 00:33:56.828
Yes. My own place.


00:33:56.830 --> 00:34:00.198
I plan to build a hut,
only for the bearded.


00:34:00.200 --> 00:34:02.066
Ruffnut, you got to stay out.


00:34:02.068 --> 00:34:03.868
Chin whiskers don't count.


00:34:03.870 --> 00:34:07.071
I see a tower of
manliness in the shape of me.


00:34:07.073 --> 00:34:10.308
It's gonna be taller than Eret
with bigger muscles.


00:34:10.310 --> 00:34:11.843
W-What?


00:34:11.845 --> 00:34:13.944
- Get out of my house!
- Hey.


00:34:13.946 --> 00:34:15.979
- Is there a problem here?
- Yeah, there's a problem.


00:34:15.981 --> 00:34:17.281
Ever since you showed up,


00:34:17.283 --> 00:34:18.850
you've been trying
to upstage me.


00:34:18.852 --> 00:34:21.051
You're just so jealous.
It's delusional.


00:34:21.053 --> 00:34:22.953
Yeah, delusion's
a good word for it.


00:34:22.955 --> 00:34:24.488
Listen, son of Eret.


00:34:24.490 --> 00:34:26.924
When Hiccup blows it as chief,
I'm next in line.


00:34:26.926 --> 00:34:29.326
Number two, 'cause
I'm clearly Valka's favorite.


00:34:29.328 --> 00:34:32.263
So, you better start
showing me some respect.


00:34:33.432 --> 00:34:34.966
Strange little man.


00:34:34.968 --> 00:34:36.734
Ah, don't mind him.


00:34:36.736 --> 00:34:40.071
It's not your fault you have
the body of a Norse god.


00:34:40.073 --> 00:34:42.107
I myself have the same problem.


00:34:43.310 --> 00:34:45.243
This one's mine.


00:34:45.245 --> 00:34:47.946
Blacksmith's stall
goes right here.


00:34:48.948 --> 00:34:51.316
One, two, three, four, five.


00:34:51.318 --> 00:34:53.951
- Where's...? Oh.
- Uh, okay.


00:34:53.953 --> 00:34:56.354
Uh, hold on, gang.
I-I said make camp.


00:34:56.356 --> 00:34:59.424
- Did you see them?
- Not build a new village.


00:34:59.426 --> 00:35:01.325
Who died and made you chief?


00:35:01.327 --> 00:35:03.995
What? Ow!


00:35:03.997 --> 00:35:06.330
Granted, this place
is very nice,


00:35:06.332 --> 00:35:08.500
but it's not the Hidden World.


00:35:08.502 --> 00:35:11.502
We don't even know
if this Hidden World exists.


00:35:11.504 --> 00:35:14.772
Yeah. This place is real.


00:35:14.774 --> 00:35:16.540
Eh, there's nothing
more stubborn


00:35:16.542 --> 00:35:19.144
than a mob of
tired, hungry Vikings.


00:35:19.146 --> 00:35:23.214
Well, I guess this can
work as a base in the meantime.


00:35:23.216 --> 00:35:26.250
It's defensible, hidden.


00:35:26.252 --> 00:35:28.520
All right. You can stay.


00:35:28.522 --> 00:35:30.254
Say hello to New Berk!


00:35:30.256 --> 00:35:32.122
Let's get building, lads.


00:35:32.124 --> 00:35:34.526
Until Toothless and I
find the Hidden World.


00:35:34.528 --> 00:35:37.060
Get off it!


00:35:37.062 --> 00:35:38.529
Now, about that voice.


00:35:38.531 --> 00:35:42.000
Can we lose the whole
honking goose thing?


00:35:42.002 --> 00:35:44.234
It's hard to imagine
wedded bliss


00:35:44.236 --> 00:35:47.171
with that going off
every minute.


00:35:47.173 --> 00:35:49.040
If you're going
to continue west,


00:35:49.042 --> 00:35:51.341
I should head back to make sure
we weren't followed.


00:35:51.343 --> 00:35:53.578
Great idea. I'll go with you
for protection.


00:35:53.580 --> 00:35:57.214
No! You're far
too important here.


00:35:57.216 --> 00:35:59.484
Yeah.


00:35:59.486 --> 00:36:01.451
Just be careful.


00:36:01.453 --> 00:36:02.953
Look at this place!
It's amazing!


00:36:02.955 --> 00:36:04.855
- That's a nice rock.
- What?


00:36:04.857 --> 00:36:09.127
This plan to hide us
from the rest of the world.


00:36:09.129 --> 00:36:11.029
Though-though I wish
it were possible,


00:36:11.031 --> 00:36:13.564
I fear it can't last, Hiccup.


00:36:13.566 --> 00:36:17.334
I mean, you know I tried
to do the same for years.


00:36:17.336 --> 00:36:22.439
But greedy humans
always find a way.


00:36:22.441 --> 00:36:26.044
I just... I only ask
that you think about it.


00:36:26.046 --> 00:36:27.377
This one's mine.


00:36:27.379 --> 00:36:29.346
I threw my axe down first.


00:36:29.348 --> 00:36:31.982
Do you still think
I'm crazy or...?


00:36:31.984 --> 00:36:36.386
Let's just say
this whole idea is very you.


00:36:36.388 --> 00:36:38.555
Well, thanks for
supporting me last night.


00:36:38.557 --> 00:36:40.091
It meant a lot.


00:36:40.093 --> 00:36:42.627
Don't thank me yet.


00:36:42.629 --> 00:36:44.595
I just hope
you're right about this.


00:36:44.597 --> 00:36:48.067
- I like it here.
- I always wanted a sunset view.


00:37:04.950 --> 00:37:07.584
Toothless.
No, it's too early.


00:38:39.745 --> 00:38:41.682
♪ ♪


00:42:07.787 --> 00:42:09.723
♪ ♪


00:42:36.783 --> 00:42:38.852
Oh, now you can draw.


00:43:59.899 --> 00:44:01.932
- Oh. Someone hasn't slept.
- Yeah.


00:44:01.934 --> 00:44:05.403
Well, that Light Fury won't
let me within a mile of her.


00:44:05.405 --> 00:44:07.404
And neither of us
will be getting any sleep


00:44:07.406 --> 00:44:10.040
or finding the Hidden World
until Toothless takes over.


00:44:10.042 --> 00:44:11.709
Hey!


00:44:11.711 --> 00:44:13.877
What do you think of that?


00:44:13.879 --> 00:44:15.812
Yeah.


00:44:15.814 --> 00:44:17.982
You tried this once before.
He didn't want it.


00:44:17.984 --> 00:44:21.451
Well, until now,
he didn't have a reason to.


00:44:21.453 --> 00:44:22.888
Right, bud?


00:44:29.928 --> 00:44:31.928
What?


00:44:31.930 --> 00:44:34.899
No, nothing.
I'm-I'm impressed.


00:44:34.901 --> 00:44:37.801
I mean, look at you.
Embracing change.


00:44:37.803 --> 00:44:39.803
I am proud of you.


00:44:39.805 --> 00:44:41.805
Well, he's my best bud.


00:44:41.807 --> 00:44:43.808
I want him to be happy.


00:44:43.810 --> 00:44:46.380
Eh, besides, it's just
until he brings her back.


00:44:50.115 --> 00:44:52.917
All right.


00:44:52.919 --> 00:44:54.655
- Fire when ready.
- Oh!


00:45:00.526 --> 00:45:03.794
Well, I guess you know
the tail is fireproof.


00:45:03.796 --> 00:45:06.529
Okay, Toothless.


00:45:06.531 --> 00:45:08.366
Okay, okay. Okay, yes, I know.


00:45:08.368 --> 00:45:09.866
I know.


00:45:09.868 --> 00:45:12.370
Okay, I know.


00:45:12.372 --> 00:45:14.705
- Please, this is not helping.
- Well, well, well.


00:45:14.707 --> 00:45:16.473
Someone's excited.


00:45:16.475 --> 00:45:18.875
He's fresh off
his first date.


00:45:18.877 --> 00:45:20.845
Now he's love crazed.


00:45:20.847 --> 00:45:23.113
Only we're the ones
going crazy.


00:45:23.115 --> 00:45:26.417
The sooner he brings back
that Light Fury, the better.


00:45:26.419 --> 00:45:28.685
Yeah, but to do that,
he'll need to fly without me.


00:45:28.687 --> 00:45:31.555
So time to give this
new and improved baby a shot.


00:45:33.459 --> 00:45:37.026
Attaboy.
Looking sharp, Toothless!


00:45:37.028 --> 00:45:39.596
So what do you think, bud?


00:45:39.598 --> 00:45:40.997
Bring her home.


00:45:40.999 --> 00:45:44.167
By sundown at the latest.


00:45:44.169 --> 00:45:46.669
No, save it
for your girlfriend.


00:45:46.671 --> 00:45:48.507
Go on. Get out of here.


00:45:55.647 --> 00:45:57.781
It's okay.


00:46:02.522 --> 00:46:04.391
♪ ♪


00:46:27.046 --> 00:46:28.749
♪ ♪


00:46:37.789 --> 00:46:39.725
♪ ♪


00:46:55.740 --> 00:46:57.076
Watch out!


00:47:00.680 --> 00:47:02.979
Go, Cloudjumper!


00:47:16.095 --> 00:47:18.162
♪ ♪


00:48:03.542 --> 00:48:06.479
♪ ♪


00:49:16.982 --> 00:49:18.984
♪ ♪


00:49:54.953 --> 00:49:56.689
♪ ♪


00:50:14.939 --> 00:50:16.839
To the chief!


00:50:16.841 --> 00:50:18.142
To the chief!


00:50:18.144 --> 00:50:20.410
Aye. To our chief.


00:50:20.412 --> 00:50:22.446
Oh, a chip off the old block.


00:50:22.448 --> 00:50:25.415
Yeah, okay, guys.
Now I'm just getting sick.


00:50:25.417 --> 00:50:27.183
Okay.


00:50:27.185 --> 00:50:29.086
Got to say,


00:50:29.088 --> 00:50:30.921
I thought you were
well off your rocker,


00:50:30.923 --> 00:50:33.089
but this spot ain't half bad.


00:50:33.091 --> 00:50:35.959
This was supposed to be
a temporary solution.


00:50:35.961 --> 00:50:36.926
It's unanimous.


00:50:36.928 --> 00:50:39.696
Everyone agrees
we've definitely traded up.


00:50:39.698 --> 00:50:42.066
Well done, Chief.


00:50:42.068 --> 00:50:43.734
What if the tail broke?


00:50:43.736 --> 00:50:45.334
What if Grimmel found him?


00:50:45.336 --> 00:50:47.937
- What if he needs me?
- Would you relax?


00:50:47.939 --> 00:50:50.107
He's probably having
the time of his life.


00:50:50.109 --> 00:50:52.341
How would I know?
She never comes around.


00:50:52.343 --> 00:50:54.812
And when she does,
she's always rushing off.


00:50:54.814 --> 00:50:57.247
I'm saying how-how do we know


00:50:57.249 --> 00:50:58.915
if she's right for us?


00:50:58.917 --> 00:51:00.917
- Us?
- You know what I mean.


00:51:00.919 --> 00:51:03.787
She's so wild and skittish.
I'm just gonna say it.


00:51:03.789 --> 00:51:04.955
I don't trust her.


00:51:04.957 --> 00:51:07.758
Can't tame 'em all, Hiccup.


00:51:07.760 --> 00:51:10.259
One day, you'll have to snip
those apron strings


00:51:10.261 --> 00:51:12.428
and let Toothless
stretch his wings.


00:51:12.430 --> 00:51:15.499
Reminds me of a talk I had
with Stoick about you.


00:51:17.803 --> 00:51:19.736
Where do they keep coming from?


00:51:19.738 --> 00:51:22.305
- Who?
- Those bloody Hobgobblers.


00:51:22.307 --> 00:51:24.941
I swear they're popping up
faster than rabbits.


00:51:24.943 --> 00:51:26.944
I think they want to eat me.


00:51:26.946 --> 00:51:29.145
Evidence would suggest
I'm tasty.


00:51:29.147 --> 00:51:30.814
Hiccy, a moment?


00:51:30.816 --> 00:51:33.816
Listen, I've been
watching you walk.


00:51:33.818 --> 00:51:35.886
Lose the limp.
No one's gonna marry that.


00:51:35.888 --> 00:51:37.754
I have a prosthetic leg.


00:51:37.756 --> 00:51:39.923
- So have I.
- And I have a parasitic twin,


00:51:39.925 --> 00:51:42.325
but you don't see me
limping around about it.


00:51:42.327 --> 00:51:45.328
Come on. Chin up, Hiccy.
Puff out that chest.


00:51:45.330 --> 00:51:47.930
Move that butt to the left a little bit.


00:51:56.107 --> 00:51:58.875
Mom, are you hurt?
W-What happened out there?


00:51:58.877 --> 00:52:01.145
I don't know how,
but Grimmel is tracking us.


00:52:01.147 --> 00:52:05.015
Ah! This is all because
of the Hobgobblers.


00:52:05.017 --> 00:52:07.116
He has a hundred ships,
maybe more,


00:52:07.118 --> 00:52:10.120
with enough cages
for all of our dragons.


00:52:11.457 --> 00:52:13.156
If Grimmel is
leading them here,


00:52:13.158 --> 00:52:15.225
we have to take him
out of the mix.


00:52:15.227 --> 00:52:18.060
Uh, and how would we do that?


00:52:18.062 --> 00:52:20.062
By going there to capture him.


00:52:20.064 --> 00:52:22.232
Capture him?


00:52:22.234 --> 00:52:24.170
I'm with him! Who else?!


00:53:10.850 --> 00:53:14.551
: Okay, split up.
We'll be harder to catch.


00:53:14.553 --> 00:53:17.120
I was thinking we should
split up, just because.


00:53:17.122 --> 00:53:19.355
I like your instincts.


00:53:19.357 --> 00:53:21.091
What is this?


00:53:45.050 --> 00:53:46.986
♪ ♪


00:54:00.198 --> 00:54:03.066
Shh! Shh! Quiet.


00:54:03.068 --> 00:54:04.634
- Quiet.
- Where's your dragon


00:54:04.636 --> 00:54:07.571
when you need him, hmm, Chief?


00:54:07.573 --> 00:54:11.174
Must have forgotten
all about you.


00:54:11.176 --> 00:54:13.243
First rule of the hunt:


00:54:13.245 --> 00:54:15.678
separate the prey
from its pack.


00:54:15.680 --> 00:54:19.683
You've just removed yourselves
from the equation.


00:54:19.685 --> 00:54:21.584
- Why are you doing this?
- Really?


00:54:21.586 --> 00:54:24.388
I didn't think you cared.


00:54:24.390 --> 00:54:27.156
Well, unlike you,
when I was a boy


00:54:27.158 --> 00:54:31.227
and I came upon a Night Fury,
I killed it where it slept.


00:54:31.229 --> 00:54:35.665
That simple act of courage
made me a hero in my village.


00:54:35.667 --> 00:54:39.201
So I decided
to kill every last one,


00:54:39.203 --> 00:54:42.673
bringing real peace
to the people of this world.


00:54:42.675 --> 00:54:44.674
Until you came along,


00:54:44.676 --> 00:54:47.944
preaching that dragons
are something other than


00:54:47.946 --> 00:54:50.113
thieves and murderers.


00:54:51.450 --> 00:54:54.984
That nonsense dies now,
starting with you.


00:54:54.986 --> 00:54:57.287
But you have dragons of your own.


00:54:57.289 --> 00:54:59.388
: These?


00:54:59.390 --> 00:55:01.390
They're dragon killers,


00:55:01.392 --> 00:55:04.660
drugged into obedience
with their own venom.


00:55:04.662 --> 00:55:07.997
Not even your precious alpha
could control them.


00:55:07.999 --> 00:55:11.334
They serve me and only me.


00:55:11.336 --> 00:55:13.703
Allow me to demonstrate.


00:55:13.705 --> 00:55:15.504
Take cover!


00:55:19.678 --> 00:55:21.477
Split up!


00:55:21.479 --> 00:55:22.915
Whoa!


00:55:28.086 --> 00:55:30.022
Whoa! Run!


00:55:48.006 --> 00:55:49.608
Up here!


00:56:05.457 --> 00:56:07.393
Hurry!


00:56:09.327 --> 00:56:11.294
Go, go, go, go, go!


00:56:13.298 --> 00:56:14.566
Hiccup!


00:56:19.805 --> 00:56:21.470
Gotcha.


00:56:21.472 --> 00:56:23.140
Go, Cloudjumper!


00:56:28.446 --> 00:56:30.446
Yeah!


00:56:30.448 --> 00:56:32.385
Our hero!


00:56:44.196 --> 00:56:45.562
Hmm.


00:56:45.564 --> 00:56:48.334
Ugh, he takes
that stupid baby everywhere.


00:56:53.671 --> 00:56:55.372
God almighty!


00:56:55.374 --> 00:56:57.307
Guess we won't be
needing this then, huh?


00:56:57.309 --> 00:56:59.575
I led us right into his trap.


00:56:59.577 --> 00:57:02.779
Yeah, nice work, Chief.
Right, Ruff?


00:57:02.781 --> 00:57:04.314
Wait.


00:57:04.316 --> 00:57:05.781
- Uh...
- Where is Ruffnut?


00:57:05.783 --> 00:57:07.651
We-we left her behind?


00:57:07.653 --> 00:57:09.685
How could you not notice
she was missing?


00:57:09.687 --> 00:57:11.520
You ride a two-headed dragon.


00:57:11.522 --> 00:57:12.689
Oh, yeah.


00:57:12.691 --> 00:57:15.792
I feel like how Ruffnut is
- dumb.


00:57:15.794 --> 00:57:17.627
Odin be spanked!


00:57:17.629 --> 00:57:19.729
This just gets
better and better.


00:57:19.731 --> 00:57:21.263
Any more fantastic news?


00:57:21.265 --> 00:57:22.598
I try to avoid looking at her.


00:57:22.600 --> 00:57:24.133
It gives me acid reflux.


00:57:24.135 --> 00:57:26.336
O-Okay, guys,
just keep your helmets on.


00:57:26.338 --> 00:57:27.803
Toothless and I will find her.


00:57:27.805 --> 00:57:29.738
Toothless has
the Light Fury now.


00:57:29.740 --> 00:57:31.508
He's probably
not even coming back.


00:57:31.510 --> 00:57:32.741
What?


00:57:32.743 --> 00:57:34.743
You gave him
his freedom, Hiccup.


00:57:34.745 --> 00:57:36.645
What were you expecting?


00:57:36.647 --> 00:57:38.515
I never thought
he'd stay away for good!


00:57:38.517 --> 00:57:41.250
I-I...


00:57:41.252 --> 00:57:44.656
Look, I'll-I'll figure it out.
I just need more time.


00:57:46.258 --> 00:57:49.191
He thinks he has to lead alone.


00:57:49.193 --> 00:57:52.729
Well, because
his father had to.


00:57:52.731 --> 00:57:56.332
He doesn't realize
the strength you have together.


00:57:56.334 --> 00:57:59.736
- Do you still believe in him?
- Of course.


00:57:59.738 --> 00:58:01.537
I wish he did.


00:58:01.539 --> 00:58:05.908
But he thinks he's nothing
without Toothless.


00:58:05.910 --> 00:58:08.580
Then help him
realize the truth.


00:58:13.218 --> 00:58:14.383
- Get on.
- What?


00:58:14.385 --> 00:58:15.618
We're going to find him.


00:58:15.620 --> 00:58:17.854
Really?


00:58:17.856 --> 00:58:21.158
Everybody, stay put.


00:58:21.160 --> 00:58:23.859
We will get Ruffnut back.
Don't worry.


00:58:23.861 --> 00:58:25.529
Worry?


00:58:25.531 --> 00:58:28.330
If they're stuck with Ruffnut,
I'm more worried about them.


00:58:30.234 --> 00:58:33.736
Why the long face?


00:58:33.738 --> 00:58:35.805
I mean, mine's long,
but yours is really long.


00:58:35.807 --> 00:58:38.575
All face and no brain, like
you got stretched at birth.


00:58:38.577 --> 00:58:40.176
Do you have a twin, too?


00:58:40.178 --> 00:58:41.912
Tuffnut took up all the room
in Mom's belly.


00:58:41.914 --> 00:58:43.779
Otherwise I'd have
a rounder head and more brains.


00:58:43.781 --> 00:58:45.915
That's science.


00:58:45.917 --> 00:58:48.317
My braids are like
little Zipplebacks. See?


00:58:50.321 --> 00:58:52.689
Even the mold spots
look like eyes. It's so cute.


00:58:52.691 --> 00:58:54.390
They even have
little horns and everything,


00:58:54.392 --> 00:58:55.725
just like Barf and Belch.


00:58:55.727 --> 00:58:57.426
Except me and Barf
can't stand Belch,


00:58:57.428 --> 00:58:58.627
so they're really just Barfs.


00:58:58.629 --> 00:58:59.696
It's warm in here.


00:58:59.698 --> 00:59:01.865
I know what you're thinking.


00:59:01.867 --> 00:59:04.667
You've never had
a prisoner this hot.


00:59:04.669 --> 00:59:06.468
All the boys love me.


00:59:06.470 --> 00:59:08.604
Except Eret,
who totally lost his chance.


00:59:08.606 --> 00:59:10.640
That ship has sailed, boy.
Sorry.


00:59:10.642 --> 00:59:11.975
And Hiccup is
practically married


00:59:11.977 --> 00:59:13.142
to that round-head, Astrid.


00:59:13.144 --> 00:59:16.513
But Snotlout and Fishlegs,
they're basically my harem.


00:59:16.515 --> 00:59:18.915
I just can't choose, you know?


00:59:18.917 --> 00:59:21.517
Snotlout's a beefcake but
almost too pretty, you know?


00:59:21.519 --> 00:59:23.852
Sometimes I think he's more
in love with himself than me.


00:59:23.854 --> 00:59:27.223
There's only room for one
beauty in this relationship.


00:59:27.225 --> 00:59:29.792
Fishlegs would keep
me alive longer if I had to


00:59:29.794 --> 00:59:31.627
eat one of them, stranded
on some glacier somewhere.


00:59:31.629 --> 00:59:33.430
But he never shuts up about dragons.


00:59:33.432 --> 00:59:34.830
Don't you hate
when people never stop talking?


00:59:34.832 --> 00:59:36.732
- Yes, I do.
- They just keep going and going.


00:59:36.734 --> 00:59:39.236
Blah, blah, blah.
It's so boring.


00:59:39.238 --> 00:59:41.238
- Can't we just feed her to your dragons?
- I'm hungry.


00:59:41.240 --> 00:59:42.638
Hey, what do you have
to eat around here?


00:59:42.640 --> 00:59:43.906
I'm allergic to fish.
You should know that.


00:59:43.908 --> 00:59:47.243
That's all they have
at that stupid new island.


00:59:47.245 --> 00:59:48.812
Do you have any clams?


00:59:48.814 --> 00:59:50.647
They're like little mouths
with slimy food inside


00:59:50.649 --> 00:59:52.749
that's already chewed,
like the way Mom used to do it.


00:59:52.751 --> 00:59:55.919
- Enough!


00:59:55.921 --> 00:59:58.354
Until I turned 12 and she was
like, "Chew your own food."


00:59:58.356 --> 00:59:59.923
And I was like,
"No, I kinda like it."


00:59:59.925 --> 01:00:02.658
Most annoying creature
ever to cross my path.


01:00:02.660 --> 01:00:04.461
Aw.


01:00:04.463 --> 01:00:07.564
Oops, you let the dragons out.


01:00:07.566 --> 01:00:09.432
I'm gonna get you.
I'm gonna get you.


01:00:09.434 --> 01:00:11.267
- No, this one's gonna get you.
- Get...


01:00:11.269 --> 01:00:13.602
Take him and go!


01:00:13.604 --> 01:00:16.339
Please! I beg you!


01:00:16.341 --> 01:00:18.741
The Deathgrippers
will have to forgo dinner.


01:00:18.743 --> 01:00:22.011
Ew, you feed
your dragons dragons?


01:00:22.013 --> 01:00:24.314
- Go!
- Where's your bathroom?


01:00:24.316 --> 01:00:25.415
I got to...


01:00:25.417 --> 01:00:27.716
Okay! Gods.


01:00:27.718 --> 01:00:30.787
No wonder you have gray hair.


01:00:30.789 --> 01:00:32.656
Stress is not good for you.


01:00:34.526 --> 01:00:36.462
So long, losers!


01:00:46.370 --> 01:00:49.004
- Where-where is she heading?
- She's tracking something.


01:00:49.006 --> 01:00:50.939
Aren't you, girl?


01:00:50.941 --> 01:00:53.942
There's nothing but
miles and miles of...


01:00:55.946 --> 01:00:57.883
♪ ♪


01:01:07.024 --> 01:01:08.961
♪ ♪


01:01:25.477 --> 01:01:27.609
A great waterfall.


01:01:27.611 --> 01:01:30.046
At the end of the world.


01:01:31.917 --> 01:01:33.853
Stormfly!


01:01:44.763 --> 01:01:46.699
♪ ♪


01:02:17.696 --> 01:02:19.632
♪ ♪


01:02:29.607 --> 01:02:31.607
Wow.


01:02:31.609 --> 01:02:33.546
Look.


01:02:42.521 --> 01:02:44.457
♪ ♪


01:03:07.812 --> 01:03:09.914
- Wow.
- Wow.


01:03:15.921 --> 01:03:17.857
♪ ♪


01:03:49.754 --> 01:03:52.254
It really does exist.


01:03:57.595 --> 01:03:59.531
♪ ♪


01:04:09.673 --> 01:04:12.508
- Toothless.
- Shh. You'll spook them.


01:04:54.852 --> 01:04:57.956
Now, that's a king.


01:05:19.810 --> 01:05:21.747
♪ ♪


01:05:39.664 --> 01:05:41.930
We should go.


01:05:41.932 --> 01:05:44.866
Oh, no.


01:05:54.044 --> 01:05:56.312
Stormfly!


01:06:12.129 --> 01:06:15.066
Go! Go!


01:06:25.943 --> 01:06:27.944
I-I'm sorry, bud.
I-I just...


01:06:37.921 --> 01:06:39.857
♪ ♪


01:06:52.903 --> 01:06:55.037
Son.


01:06:56.207 --> 01:06:57.874
You should be asleep.


01:06:57.876 --> 01:07:00.178
I was thirsty.


01:07:03.281 --> 01:07:05.017
Yeah, come here.


01:07:16.260 --> 01:07:18.694
Dad?


01:07:18.696 --> 01:07:22.330
Are you gonna get us a new mom?


01:07:25.303 --> 01:07:27.035
I don't want another.


01:07:27.037 --> 01:07:31.273
Your mom was
the only woman for me.


01:07:31.275 --> 01:07:33.945
She was the love of my life.


01:07:35.879 --> 01:07:40.082
But with love comes loss, son.


01:07:40.084 --> 01:07:41.951
It's part of the deal.


01:07:41.953 --> 01:07:46.691
Sometimes it hurts, but
in the end, it's all worth it.


01:07:49.394 --> 01:07:52.862
There's no greater gift
than love.


01:08:19.524 --> 01:08:22.928
♪ ♪


01:08:35.172 --> 01:08:37.439
It's okay, bud.


01:08:37.441 --> 01:08:39.845
You belong there, with her.


01:08:41.546 --> 01:08:43.045
We don't.


01:08:45.415 --> 01:08:48.850
And that's all right.


01:08:48.852 --> 01:08:51.153
We'll find a way to man...


01:09:00.330 --> 01:09:01.997
Hey!


01:09:03.168 --> 01:09:06.935
She followed us back!


01:09:10.240 --> 01:09:13.377
We might not have to
say good-bye after all.


01:09:20.851 --> 01:09:22.184
That's it.


01:09:22.186 --> 01:09:23.986
Woo-hoo! Yeah!


01:09:23.988 --> 01:09:26.022
- Ruffnut?
- Miss me?


01:09:26.024 --> 01:09:27.490
How did you escape?


01:09:27.492 --> 01:09:29.224
I annoyed them
till they let me go.


01:09:29.226 --> 01:09:30.893
Wait. Wait.


01:09:30.895 --> 01:09:33.996
- Grimmel let you go?
- So dumb.


01:09:33.998 --> 01:09:35.997
They couldn't handle me.


01:09:35.999 --> 01:09:38.000
See, everyone thinks
Tuffnut's more annoying, but...


01:09:38.002 --> 01:09:40.303
- Wait, hold on.
- Ruffnut, focus.


01:09:40.305 --> 01:09:42.170
Were you followed?


01:09:42.172 --> 01:09:44.240
I never look back, Hiccup.


01:09:44.242 --> 01:09:46.341
Toothless.


01:09:46.343 --> 01:09:48.844
Toothless!


01:09:59.990 --> 01:10:01.793
Toothless, come back!


01:10:10.235 --> 01:10:11.570
No!


01:10:28.218 --> 01:10:33.054
And now our little game
must come to an end.


01:10:37.328 --> 01:10:39.194
Call them off, alpha!


01:10:39.196 --> 01:10:41.999
No reason for her to die, too.


01:10:55.212 --> 01:10:56.478
What are they doing?


01:10:56.480 --> 01:11:00.215
- They could totally take him.
- Not with her life on the line.


01:11:03.421 --> 01:11:04.987
Save your breath.


01:11:04.989 --> 01:11:08.291
The only alpha
they respond to is me.


01:11:13.263 --> 01:11:15.197
Oh...


01:11:15.199 --> 01:11:18.099
don't feel too badly.
You tried your best.


01:11:18.101 --> 01:11:23.005
But you are nothing
without your dragon.


01:11:38.088 --> 01:11:39.455
Toothless!


01:11:57.374 --> 01:11:59.608
Oh, that is
just great!


01:11:59.610 --> 01:12:00.776
Now what?


01:12:00.778 --> 01:12:04.346
I think it's time for number
two to become number one.


01:12:04.348 --> 01:12:06.284
He'll listen to you.


01:12:11.288 --> 01:12:13.555
- Don't say it.
- I wasn't going to.


01:12:13.557 --> 01:12:15.291
I shouldn't have
dragged you out there.


01:12:15.293 --> 01:12:17.526
He wouldn't have flown me back.
She wouldn't have followed.


01:12:17.528 --> 01:12:19.527
Yep.


01:12:19.529 --> 01:12:22.497
I feel like the same screwup
I was before I met Toothless.


01:12:22.499 --> 01:12:24.332
I can see that.


01:12:24.334 --> 01:12:26.501
Are you just gonna stand there
and agree with everything?


01:12:26.503 --> 01:12:27.335
Well, you're right.


01:12:27.337 --> 01:12:30.171
You're back
to where you started,


01:12:30.173 --> 01:12:32.508
but I was the first
to believe in you.


01:12:32.510 --> 01:12:34.210
And I have watched you doubt


01:12:34.212 --> 01:12:36.679
whether you're worthy
ever since.


01:12:36.681 --> 01:12:38.514
But you know what?


01:12:38.516 --> 01:12:42.385
I am the person I am today
because of you.


01:12:42.387 --> 01:12:45.453
I never told you that,
but it's true.


01:12:45.455 --> 01:12:48.157
You are the bravest,
most stubborn,


01:12:48.159 --> 01:12:52.161
most determined knucklehead
I know.


01:12:52.163 --> 01:12:54.429
Toothless didn't
give you that, Hiccup.


01:12:54.431 --> 01:12:57.767
- He just made it...
- Easier.


01:12:57.769 --> 01:13:01.370
And now it's gonna be
a lot harder.


01:13:01.372 --> 01:13:04.807
So, what are you
gonna do about it?


01:13:04.809 --> 01:13:07.542
Probably something stupid.


01:13:07.544 --> 01:13:10.315
That's the Hiccup I know.


01:13:13.418 --> 01:13:16.318
Suit up, gang.
We're going to get them back.


01:13:16.320 --> 01:13:19.321
- What?
- He's lost his mind.


01:13:19.323 --> 01:13:22.425
Now, that's marriage material.


01:13:22.427 --> 01:13:25.661
At last, faithful pupil,
you are ready.


01:13:25.663 --> 01:13:30.832
Um, how are we gonna get our
dragons back without dragons?


01:13:30.834 --> 01:13:32.201
Trust me.


01:13:35.806 --> 01:13:38.273
- Watch yourselves.
- You're next.


01:13:39.843 --> 01:13:41.210
Move it.


01:13:44.082 --> 01:13:46.348
Um, that's right, alpha.


01:13:46.350 --> 01:13:48.320
No surprises.


01:13:56.694 --> 01:14:02.264
So, jump off the cliff
in these.


01:14:02.266 --> 01:14:03.765
That's the best you've got?


01:14:03.767 --> 01:14:06.568
No, you guys are
the best I've got.


01:14:06.570 --> 01:14:08.837
Aw.


01:14:08.839 --> 01:14:10.605
- I'm with him! Who else?!
- I'm with...


01:14:10.607 --> 01:14:12.640
Ruffnut, that was my line.


01:14:12.642 --> 01:14:14.643
- Let's go!
- Try to keep up!


01:14:18.783 --> 01:14:20.349
Yeah! - Yeah!


01:14:20.351 --> 01:14:23.118
- I'm doing it!
- All right! - Oh!


01:14:23.120 --> 01:14:24.385
Get clear!


01:14:33.196 --> 01:14:35.497
Aw.


01:14:35.499 --> 01:14:37.666
You didn't think I'd actually
hand you the Night Fury,


01:14:37.668 --> 01:14:38.666
did you?


01:14:38.668 --> 01:14:40.368
He's mine to kill.


01:14:40.370 --> 01:14:42.170
That snake!


01:14:42.172 --> 01:14:44.874
I intend to finish
what I started.


01:14:44.876 --> 01:14:49.210
Best of luck controlling them
without an alpha.


01:14:49.212 --> 01:14:51.482
Hold on, Toothless!


01:14:54.918 --> 01:14:57.286
Let go!


01:14:57.288 --> 01:14:58.786
Could've used
some practice!


01:14:58.788 --> 01:15:00.889
Ah, I should've
skipped breakfast!


01:15:11.269 --> 01:15:12.701
Toothless!


01:15:14.872 --> 01:15:17.273
Look out!


01:15:17.275 --> 01:15:19.308
Hot, hot, hot, hot!


01:15:21.212 --> 01:15:24.380
They're getting away!


01:15:33.423 --> 01:15:35.691
Perfect timing.


01:15:35.693 --> 01:15:38.359
- Put that down!
- I'll take the skinny one!


01:15:38.361 --> 01:15:39.361
Game faces!


01:15:39.363 --> 01:15:42.197
Yeah, what are you waiting for?
Get in there.


01:15:42.199 --> 01:15:43.432
Yeah!


01:15:43.434 --> 01:15:45.837
Take that!


01:15:52.677 --> 01:15:54.713
Ah.


01:16:12.529 --> 01:16:13.728
- Watch out!
- The dragons are everywhere!


01:16:13.730 --> 01:16:15.496
- Incoming!
- Here they come!


01:16:15.498 --> 01:16:17.966
Incoming!


01:16:17.968 --> 01:16:19.501
Take cover!


01:16:19.503 --> 01:16:21.737
Where are you going?!


01:16:25.443 --> 01:16:28.243
- Heads up!
- - Thanks.


01:16:28.245 --> 01:16:29.181
Look out!


01:16:32.315 --> 01:16:34.251
Thanks.


01:16:59.377 --> 01:17:01.477
I'm coming, Toothless!


01:17:01.479 --> 01:17:04.580
You still think
he cares about you?


01:17:05.949 --> 01:17:09.787
Let's just see who he follows.


01:17:21.899 --> 01:17:24.032
I'm sorry, bud, for everything.


01:17:43.087 --> 01:17:45.022
Now, let's go get her.


01:17:48.525 --> 01:17:50.925
Woo-hoo! Yeah!


01:17:50.927 --> 01:17:52.460
Number two coming through!


01:17:52.462 --> 01:17:54.028
Surprise!


01:17:54.030 --> 01:17:55.496
Sorry about that.


01:17:55.498 --> 01:17:57.465
Come on.


01:17:58.869 --> 01:18:02.837
- All right!
- One more free! Four to go!


01:18:04.708 --> 01:18:06.742
Try to keep up!


01:18:06.744 --> 01:18:09.044
I got your backs. Oh!


01:18:10.580 --> 01:18:13.648
Yeah, it's almost like
we're a team.


01:18:16.553 --> 01:18:19.587
You brought a baby to a battle.


01:18:19.589 --> 01:18:22.657
Ah-ah-ah. I wouldn't
do that if I were you.


01:18:32.535 --> 01:18:35.002
God, I love that dragon.


01:18:35.004 --> 01:18:38.139
Come on! Come back here!


01:18:40.110 --> 01:18:42.111
Sorry we're late for the party.


01:18:42.113 --> 01:18:43.948
You're right on time.


01:18:53.656 --> 01:18:55.694
That's it. That's it.


01:19:06.669 --> 01:19:09.404
How are we gonna get him off
her back without hurting her?


01:19:09.406 --> 01:19:11.740
Fear the facial hair!


01:19:20.650 --> 01:19:22.184
- Oh, I have missed this.
- Me, too.


01:19:22.186 --> 01:19:24.185
Oh!


01:19:24.187 --> 01:19:25.787
Ooh. See that there?


01:19:25.789 --> 01:19:27.822
Aw. Cute.


01:19:27.824 --> 01:19:30.626
That's a bad omen.
You're cursed.


01:19:36.766 --> 01:19:38.533
Yes! Go on!


01:19:38.535 --> 01:19:39.801
Good on you!


01:19:39.803 --> 01:19:42.136
I guess you're not
so bad after all.


01:20:04.794 --> 01:20:06.828
Abandon ship!


01:20:06.830 --> 01:20:08.697
Whoa!


01:20:16.140 --> 01:20:17.505
- Yay!
- Oh, that was awesome!


01:20:17.507 --> 01:20:20.576
Yeah!


01:20:20.578 --> 01:20:23.013
♪ ♪


01:20:25.114 --> 01:20:28.051
Uh, we've got problems.


01:20:42.766 --> 01:20:45.970
Take him down, Hiccup!


01:20:55.044 --> 01:20:57.815
We need a better plan,
and quick!


01:21:02.186 --> 01:21:04.620
Uh, uh, what are,
what are you doing?


01:21:04.622 --> 01:21:08.023
Okay. Okay.


01:21:16.766 --> 01:21:18.267
Where has he gone?


01:21:33.650 --> 01:21:35.149
You'll kill both of us!


01:21:35.151 --> 01:21:37.618
Fighting over a dragon?


01:21:37.620 --> 01:21:39.054
That's your plan?


01:21:42.092 --> 01:21:44.693
This is.


01:21:47.830 --> 01:21:49.766
Save him.


01:22:07.117 --> 01:22:09.686
♪ ♪


01:22:25.903 --> 01:22:28.205
No!


01:22:33.910 --> 01:22:35.309
See?


01:22:35.311 --> 01:22:37.681
I knew you'd come around.


01:22:57.266 --> 01:22:59.102
Yeah!


01:23:13.350 --> 01:23:15.349
Hey. Good morning, bud.


01:23:17.354 --> 01:23:19.955
Here you go.


01:23:19.957 --> 01:23:22.758
Boy, you're full of surprises.


01:23:24.160 --> 01:23:27.194
He's all yours.


01:23:38.342 --> 01:23:40.942
You know, Eret may be
blessed with brawn,


01:23:40.944 --> 01:23:44.845
but, just between us,
you have the brains.


01:23:44.847 --> 01:23:47.115
Number one.


01:23:47.117 --> 01:23:49.052
♪ ♪


01:24:18.915 --> 01:24:21.785
You're right, bud.
It's time.


01:24:23.454 --> 01:24:28.322
I was so busy fighting for
a world that I wanted,


01:24:28.324 --> 01:24:31.361
I didn't think about
what you needed.


01:24:34.464 --> 01:24:38.066
You've looked after us
for long enough.


01:24:38.068 --> 01:24:40.238
Time to look after yourselves.


01:24:53.883 --> 01:24:57.219
Oh, Stormfly, my good girl.


01:24:57.221 --> 01:24:58.487
All right, Grumpy.


01:24:58.489 --> 01:25:01.490
Off you go.


01:25:01.492 --> 01:25:04.792
So long, you big ugly beast.


01:25:04.794 --> 01:25:05.993
I'll miss you.


01:25:09.199 --> 01:25:12.200
♪ ♪


01:25:14.805 --> 01:25:17.408
Oh, Cloudjumper. Oh.


01:25:26.150 --> 01:25:28.149
Go on, bud.


01:25:28.151 --> 01:25:30.318
Lead them to the Hidden World.


01:25:32.256 --> 01:25:34.456
You'll be safe there.


01:25:34.458 --> 01:25:37.959
Safer than you could
ever be with me.


01:25:39.128 --> 01:25:41.129
It's okay.
I love you, too.


01:25:41.131 --> 01:25:42.831
And I want you to be free.


01:25:46.503 --> 01:25:49.203
Our world doesn't deserve you.


01:25:49.205 --> 01:25:50.475
Yet.


01:26:01.885 --> 01:26:03.320
Go, Toothless.


01:26:05.388 --> 01:26:07.024
Go.


01:26:10.293 --> 01:26:12.229
♪ ♪


01:26:49.867 --> 01:26:53.104
♪ ♪


01:27:19.262 --> 01:27:21.198
♪ ♪


01:27:39.283 --> 01:27:41.218
♪ ♪


01:28:01.305 --> 01:28:03.240
♪ ♪


01:28:33.302 --> 01:28:36.036
To the chief and chieftess!


01:28:36.038 --> 01:28:38.605
Yeah!


01:28:38.607 --> 01:28:40.508
Good on you!


01:28:40.510 --> 01:28:43.978
Come, cry into
my full, thick beard.


01:28:43.980 --> 01:28:46.246
It's so beautiful!


01:28:46.248 --> 01:28:48.483
Gross.


01:28:48.485 --> 01:28:50.652
Okay, you win.


01:28:50.654 --> 01:28:53.153
I like sensitive guys.


01:28:53.155 --> 01:28:54.990
I thought
it would never happen.


01:28:54.992 --> 01:28:56.523
Finally, right?


01:28:58.528 --> 01:29:00.463
♪ ♪


01:29:26.757 --> 01:29:29.390
<i>There were dragons
when I was a boy.</i>


01:29:32.395 --> 01:29:34.728
<i>Ah, there were
great, grim sky dragons</i>


01:29:34.730 --> 01:29:38.800
<i>that nested on the clifftops
like gigantic, scary birds.</i>


01:29:40.169 --> 01:29:41.635
<i>Little, brown, scuttly dragons</i>


01:29:41.637 --> 01:29:46.241
<i>that hunted down the mice and
rats in well-organized packs.</i>


01:29:46.243 --> 01:29:48.675
<i>Preposterously huge sea dragons</i>


01:29:48.677 --> 01:29:53.648
<i>that were 20 times as big
as the big blue whale.</i>


01:29:53.650 --> 01:29:56.151
<i>Some say they crawled
back into the sea,</i>


01:29:56.153 --> 01:29:59.754
<i>leaving not a bone nor a fang
for men to remember them by.</i>


01:29:59.756 --> 01:30:04.459
<i>Others say they were nothing
but folktales to begin with.</i>


01:30:04.461 --> 01:30:06.998
<i>Ah, I'm okay with that.</i>


01:30:28.150 --> 01:30:30.218
Hey.


01:30:30.220 --> 01:30:32.556
Hey there, bud.


01:30:39.128 --> 01:30:40.631
Remember me?


01:30:43.100 --> 01:30:44.735
It's okay.


01:30:54.377 --> 01:30:58.345
Hey, I am glad
to see you, too, bud.


01:30:58.347 --> 01:31:00.782
He's not gonna eat your father.


